    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0309" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/1792a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-21T18:00:00-05:00">April 21, 1941—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. For Kirk from Feis.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d249-f1"/> Much interested and will
                    follow matter through vigorously. An arrangement might be facilitated if
                    estimates were transmitted at once of immediately available supplies
                    particularly of manganese, tungsten and wolfram, with particulars as to
                    grades.</p>
                <p>You are much in our thoughts. [Feis.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d249-f1" n="43" xml:id="d249-f1-content">
                <p>Herbert Feis, Adviser on International Economic Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
